-- חוזר לבעלויות תש"ף/1 (30.7.2019): חוזר העסקת עו"ה, עובדי בעלות, בבתי ספר
-- לחינוך מיוחד מוכרים שאינם רשמיים, בהתאם לרפורמת אופק חדש בשנה"ל תש"ף.
-- Applying the Ofek Hadash reform from תש"ף to the owners' teaching
-- employees in recognised-unofficial special-education schools: who joins,
-- the work week, part and excess positions, mothers, age hours, principals
-- and deputies, promotion, counsellors, grade conversion, salary advances,
-- the attendance clock — and the annexed forms and conversion examples.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common
IMPORT daydate

§ `תש"ף/1 העסקת עו"ה בבתי ספר לחינוך מיוחד מוכרים שאינם רשמיים באופק חדש`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, date, reference number, circular number, addressee (owners of recognised-unofficial special-education schools), greeting and subject line; no rule.

-- Throughout, "the employer" is the owning body (הבעלות) that employs the
-- teaching employees; the Ministry is the Ministry of Education.

§§ `1 Introduction`

-- akn:art_1/p1 akn:art_1/p2 The background: the State's undertaking in HCJ 148/18 to equalise teaching resources, and the inter-ministerial team whose conclusions the Director-General adopted; no rule.
-- akn:art_1/p3 akn:art_1/p4 akn:art_1/p5 Where the team's report is published (a link); no rule.
-- akn:art_1/p8 The circular's purpose: to explain the instructions for owners' teaching employees in these schools; no rule.

-- §1 ¶6: from תש"ף the terms of Ofek Hadash apply to the recognised-unofficial
-- special-education schools. School years are counted by their first
-- calendar year (תש"ף = 2019).
@ref akn:art_1/p6
GIVEN `recognised-unofficial special-education school` IS A BOOLEAN, `school year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Ofek Hadash applies to the school` `recognised-unofficial special-education school` `school year` IF
    `recognised-unofficial special-education school` AND `school year` AT LEAST 2019

-- §1 ¶7 (and §14.1, annex E ¶5): the Ministry alone approves joining, sets
-- the Ofek Hadash grade and converts the salary; it also sets the education
-- grade and the teaching seniority.
@ref akn:art_1/p7 akn:art_14__para_14-1/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1/p5
GIVEN d IS A `determination`
GIVETH A Party
DECIDE `who determines` d IS `the Ministry of Education`

DECLARE `determination` IS ONE OF
    `approval of joining Ofek Hadash`
    `the Ofek Hadash grade`
    `the salary conversion`
    `the education grade`
    `teaching seniority`

§§ `2 Responsibilities in applying the reform`

DECLARE `reform action` IS ONE OF
    `sign the commitment to apply Ofek Hadash`
    `check and update the teaching employees' data`
    `follow up the fulfilment of the degree commitment`
    `employ an intern other than on reform terms`
    `report working hours manually`
    `instruct unreported teachers to open an online teacher file`
    `identify the teachers who meet the joining conditions`
    `employ eligible teachers on Ofek Hadash terms and work week`
    `attend the pedagogical training conferences`
    `guide teachers in opening an online file`
    `set a timetable by the Ofek Hadash work week`
    `place every teaching employee in the placement system`
    `transfer the salary interface to the Ministry's contractor`
    `pay Ofek Hadash salary from joining and deduct the advances` HAS `months back to joining` IS A NUMBER
    `decide each teacher's joining`
    `set each joined teacher's grade`
    `compute the school's Ofek Hadash profile`
    `reimburse the owner`
    `pay the Ofek Hadash advance` HAS `advance paid` IS A NUMBER
    `report working hours by the attendance clock`
    `pay and deduct by the attendance clock`
    `install an attendance clock`
    `apply to leave Ofek Hadash on the annex D form`

-- §2.1(1): until the regulations on recognised institutions are amended, the
-- owner commits to apply Ofek Hadash to its special-education schools, on
-- the form of annex A (also at the link). Annex A: the owner applies from
-- תש"ף every provision of the Ofek Hadash agreement of 25.12.2008, as
-- updated, that concerns a special-education school — the work week, the
-- salary and the pedagogical instructions — on pain of sanctions up to the
-- revocation of its licence.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1/p1 akn:art_2__para_2-1/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p1 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p3 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p4 akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 akn:att_1__hc_1/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1/p3 akn:att_1__hc_1/p4 akn:att_1__hc_1/p5 akn:att_1__hc_1/p6
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `the owner's commitment` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `sign the commitment to apply Ofek Hadash`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תש\"ף/1 §2.1(1), annex A: failing the commitment may bring sanctions up to revocation of the licence"

-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p7 akn:att_1__hc_1/p8 akn:att_1__hc_1/p9 akn:att_1__hc_1/p10 akn:att_1__hc_1/p11 Annex A's blank table of institutions, signature and date lines; a form, no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p12 akn:att_1__hc_1/p13 akn:att_1__hc_1/p14 akn:att_1__hc_1/p15 The letterhead of the next page; no rule.

-- §2.1(2): the staff report in the עוש"ר system lists the teachers as reported
-- for תשע"ט; (א) the owner checks the data (education, seniority, military
-- or national service, training rewards, double degree) and has corrections
-- sent through a contact to the district; (ב) teachers not yet reported —
-- health professions and arts therapists included — are told to open an
-- online teacher file at once, by the circular on candidates for תש"ף.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2/p1 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_a/p1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `checking the teachers' data` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `check and update the teaching employees' data`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תש\"ף/1 §2.1(2)(א): the teaching employees' data are checked and brought up to date"

@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p1 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p3 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p4 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p5
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `opening files for unreported teachers` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `instruct unreported teachers to open an online teacher file`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תש\"ף/1 §2.1(2)(ב): unreported teachers are told to open an online file urgently"

-- §2.1(3)–(4): the owner identifies the teachers who meet §3's conditions and
-- employs them on Ofek Hadash pay and work week (§4).
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_3/p1 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_4/p1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `employing the eligible teachers` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `identify the teachers who meet the joining conditions`
    HENCE PARTY `the employer`
          MUST  `employ eligible teachers on Ofek Hadash terms and work week`
          LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תש\"ף/1 §2.1(4): eligible teachers are employed on Ofek Hadash terms"
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תש\"ף/1 §2.1(3): the eligible teachers are identified"

-- §2.1(4) ¶2 and (1)–(4): the principal attends the training conferences,
-- guides teachers in opening online files, sets the timetable by the Ofek
-- Hadash work week, and places every teacher — joined or not — in the
-- placement system (instructions on placement follow separately).
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_4/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_4__cls_1/p1 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_4__cls_2/p1 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_4__cls_3/p1 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_4__cls_4/p1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `the principal's actions` IS
        (PARTY `the school principal` MUST `attend the pedagogical training conferences`)
    RAND (PARTY `the school principal` MUST `guide teachers in opening an online file`)
    RAND (PARTY `the school principal` MUST `set a timetable by the Ofek Hadash work week`)
    RAND (PARTY `the school principal` MUST `place every teaching employee in the placement system`)

-- §2.2: to set the initial grade the owner sends the Ministry's contractor
-- (Unique) the salary interface for the month asked; the Ministry sets the
-- grade and converts. Once the grade is set, the owner pays Ofek Hadash
-- salary from the teacher's joining and deducts the advances of §15.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-2/p1 akn:art_2__para_2-2/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_1/p1 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p1
GIVEN `months since joining` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `paying from the grade` `months since joining` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `transfer the salary interface to the Ministry's contractor`
    HENCE PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
          MUST  `set each joined teacher's grade`
          HENCE PARTY `the employer`
                MUST  `pay Ofek Hadash salary from joining and deduct the advances` `months back to joining`
                      PROVIDED `months back to joining` AT LEAST `months since joining`
                LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תש\"ף/1 §2.2(2): salary by the grade from the joining date, the advances deducted"
          LEST BREACH BY `the Ministry of Education` BECAUSE "תש\"ף/1 §2.2: the Ministry sets the grade"
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תש\"ף/1 §2.2(1): the salary interface is sent to the Ministry's contractor"

-- §2.2 ¶2–9: the Ministry decides each teacher's joining, sets the grades,
-- computes the school's Ofek Hadash profile and reimburses the owner by the
-- approved teachers, pay and work week — and cannot reimburse without the
-- placement system updated to the Ofek Hadash week and the salary interface.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p3 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p4 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p5 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p6 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p7 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p8 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p9
GIVEN `placement system updated to the Ofek Hadash week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `salary interface transferred`                    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `the Ministry's actions` `placement system updated to the Ofek Hadash week` `salary interface transferred` IS
        (PARTY `the Ministry of Education` MUST `decide each teacher's joining`)
    RAND (PARTY `the Ministry of Education` MUST `set each joined teacher's grade`)
    RAND (PARTY `the Ministry of Education` MUST `compute the school's Ofek Hadash profile`)
    RAND (IF `the Ministry can reimburse the owner` `placement system updated to the Ofek Hadash week` `salary interface transferred`
          THEN PARTY `the Ministry of Education` MUST `reimburse the owner`
          ELSE FULFILLED)

GIVEN `placement system updated to the Ofek Hadash week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `salary interface transferred`                    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ministry can reimburse the owner` `placement system updated to the Ofek Hadash week` `salary interface transferred` IF
    `placement system updated to the Ofek Hadash week` AND `salary interface transferred`

§§ `3 Joining conditions`

@desc A teaching employee of the owner, as far as joining Ofek Hadash asks.
DECLARE `special-ed teacher` HAS
    `previously recognised teaching seniority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc years of actual teaching recognised from a non-state employer or in the state service, other than internship, army or national service in teaching
    `entitled to seniority recognition for actual teaching` IS A BOOLEAN
    `academic`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc holds an academic degree, or a salary grade the Ministry approved as equivalent to an academic one
    `certified to teach`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc holds a teaching certificate or certification
    `position fraction`           IS A NUMBER
    `seniority years`             IS A NUMBER  @desc teaching seniority in years, months as a fraction
    `intern`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc in the internship (stage) year
    `health profession or arts therapist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc occupational therapy, physiotherapy or speech therapy; or therapy through visual art, movement, drama, music, bibliotherapy or psychodrama
    `in regular education`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc a teacher in regular (not special) education, for section 3.4's bracket
    `signed the degree commitment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc signed annex C's commitment to complete an academic degree within 4 years
    `exception approved by the committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the exceptions committee approved joining without a teaching certificate

-- §3.1.1–3.1.2: a NEW teacher has no previously recognised seniority in
-- actual teaching (internship, army or national service in teaching aside);
-- an EXISTING teacher is entitled to seniority recognition for actual teaching.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_3-1-1/p1
GIVEN t IS A `special-ed teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a new teacher` t IF (NOT t's `previously recognised teaching seniority`)

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_3-1-2/p1
GIVEN t IS A `special-ed teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing teacher` t IF t's `entitled to seniority recognition for actual teaching`

-- §3.2.1: an existing academic teacher joins if certified to teach and
-- employed at a third of a position or more; without a certificate, only by
-- the exceptions committee (form of annex B, via the "Shaar" portal).
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-2/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p3 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p4 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p5 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p6 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p7 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p8
GIVEN t IS A `special-ed teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing academic teacher joins` t IF
        `an existing teacher` t
    AND t's `academic`
    AND t's `position fraction` AT LEAST 1 DIVIDED BY 3
    AND (t's `certified to teach` OR t's `exception approved by the committee`)

-- Annex B: the request to join by exception; the teacher acknowledges no
-- grade advance until certified, and Ofek Hadash terms from signing.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1 Annex B, the form requesting exceptional joining (personal and institution details, the request, the acknowledgements of sections 3.2.1 and 12.2.2, signature, the portal link and the next page's letterhead); a form restating rules encoded at those sections.

-- §3.2.1 ¶9–10 and §12.2.2: an uncertified teacher with under 25 years'
-- seniority cannot advance a grade until certified; the time worked and part
-- of the studies count toward advancement (§12.2.2).
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p9 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p10
GIVEN t IS A `special-ed teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `barred from advancing until certified under §3.2.1` t IF
    (NOT t's `certified to teach`) AND t's `seniority years` LESS THAN 25

-- §3.3.1–3.3.2: an existing non-academic teacher with up to 27 years
-- (inclusive) joins only on signing the commitment (annex C) to complete an
-- academic degree within 4 years of signing; one with 28 years and more
-- need not sign and is employed on reform terms regardless.
-- F-2019-20_tashaf_01-a: seniority above 27 and below 28 is in neither.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-1/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-1/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-1/p3 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-2/p1
GIVEN t IS A `special-ed teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must sign the degree commitment` t IF
    `an existing teacher` t AND (NOT t's `academic`) AND t's `seniority years` AT MOST 27

GIVEN t IS A `special-ed teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `joins without a commitment` t IF
    `an existing teacher` t AND (NOT t's `academic`) AND t's `seniority years` AT LEAST 28

-- Reading adopted (F-2019-20_tashaf_01-a): the bands count completed years,
-- so a teacher who has not completed 28 years is "up to 27" and must sign.
GIVEN t IS A `special-ed teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must sign, counting completed years` t IF
    `an existing teacher` t AND (NOT t's `academic`) AND t's `seniority years` LESS THAN 28

GIVEN t IS A `special-ed teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing non-academic teacher joins` t IF
       (`must sign, counting completed years` t AND t's `signed the degree commitment`)
    OR `joins without a commitment` t

-- §3.3.3: the commitment's fulfilment is followed up.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-3/p1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `following up the commitments` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `follow up the fulfilment of the degree commitment`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תש\"ף/1 §3.3.3: the fulfilment of the degree commitment is followed up"

-- §3.3.4: proof of a degree within 4 years of JOINING brings the salary
-- differences retroactively from joining; later, the academic table without
-- differences. Annex C: the teacher commits to finish within 4 years of
-- SIGNING, and is told that finishing within 4 years of joining brings
-- differences retroactively from SIGNING. F-2019-20_tashaf_01-b.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-4/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-4/p2
GIVEN joined IS A DATE, completed IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `differences are due under §3.3.4` joined completed IF
    completed AT MOST `four years after` joined

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `four years after` d IS DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY d) (DATE_MONTH d) (DATE_YEAR d PLUS 4)

-- Annex C ¶9: the teacher commits to finish within 4 years of SIGNING.
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1/p9
GIVEN signed IS A DATE, completed IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the commitment of annex C is kept` signed completed IF
    completed AT MOST `four years after` signed

-- Annex C ¶10: finishing within 4 years of JOINING brings the differences
-- retroactively from the date of SIGNING (F-2019-20_tashaf_01-b).
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1/p10
GIVEN joined IS A DATE, signed IS A DATE, completed IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `annex C's differences run from` joined signed completed IS
    IF completed AT MOST `four years after` joined
    THEN JUST signed
    ELSE NOTHING


-- Annex C ¶11–16: an academic degree is one from a recognised Israeli
-- institution of higher education, one from abroad recognised as equivalent
-- by the Ministry's evaluation unit, or studies earning a salary grade
-- approved as equivalent to an academic one.
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1/p11 akn:att_3__hc_1/p12 akn:att_3__hc_1/p13 akn:att_3__hc_1/p14 akn:att_3__hc_1/p15 akn:att_3__hc_1/p16
GIVEN q IS A `qualification`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an academic degree for annex C` q IF
    NOT (q EQUALS `other studies`)

DECLARE `qualification` IS ONE OF
    `degree from a recognised Israeli institution`
    `foreign degree recognised as equivalent`
    `studies earning an approved academic-equivalent grade`
    `other studies`

-- akn:att_3__hc_1/p1 akn:att_3__hc_1/p2 akn:att_3__hc_1/p3 akn:att_3__hc_1/p4 akn:att_3__hc_1/p5 akn:att_3__hc_1/p6 akn:att_3__hc_1/p7 akn:att_3__hc_1/p8 Annex C's title and personal and institution details; a form, no rule.
-- akn:att_3__hc_1/p17 akn:att_3__hc_1/p18 akn:att_3__hc_1/p19 akn:att_3__hc_1/p20 akn:att_3__hc_1/p21 akn:att_3__hc_1/p22 akn:att_3__hc_1/p23 akn:att_3__hc_1/p24 Annex C's acknowledgement that reform terms apply only once signed (as section 3.3.1 says), signature, link and letterhead; no further rule.

-- §3.4: a new academic teacher in special education joins if certified and
-- employed at a third of a position or more (half in regular education).
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p3 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p4 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p5 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p6 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p7
GIVEN t IS A `special-ed teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a new academic teacher joins` t IF
        `a new teacher` t
    AND t's `academic`
    AND t's `certified to teach`
    AND t's `position fraction` AT LEAST (IF t's `in regular education` THEN 0.5 ELSE 1 DIVIDED BY 3)

-- §3.5: in a reform school interns are employed only on reform terms; the
-- year counts only at a third of a position or more; the internship lasts at
-- most two years, within which the degree and certificate are completed or
-- reform employment stops; it counts for tenure, jubilee and recuperation
-- seniority, not for salary seniority or the minimum time to promotion.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-1/p1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `employing interns on reform terms only` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    SHANT `employ an intern other than on reform terms`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תש\"ף/1 §3.5.1: in a school joined to Ofek Hadash interns are employed only on reform terms"

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-1/p1
GIVEN t IS A `special-ed teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internship year is recognised` t IF
    t's `intern` AND t's `position fraction` AT LEAST 1 DIVIDED BY 3

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-2/p1
GIVEN `years of internship` IS A NUMBER, `degree and certificate completed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an intern may go on under reform terms` `years of internship` `degree and certificate completed` IF
    `years of internship` AT MOST 2 OR `degree and certificate completed`

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-3/p1
GIVEN p IS A `seniority purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internship counts for` p IF
    NOT (p EQUALS `salary seniority` OR p EQUALS `minimum time to promotion`)

DECLARE `seniority purpose` IS ONE OF
    `salary seniority`
    `minimum time to promotion`
    `tenure`
    `jubilee grant seniority`
    `recuperation seniority`

-- §3.6: a substitute employed in weekly hours takes the employment features
-- of the teacher replaced.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-6/p1 akn:art_3__para_3-6/p2
GIVEN `the replaced teacher's terms` IS A STRING, `employed in weekly hours` IS A BOOLEAN, `own terms` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `a substitute's terms` `the replaced teacher's terms` `employed in weekly hours` `own terms` IS
    IF `employed in weekly hours` THEN `the replaced teacher's terms` ELSE `own terms`

§§ `4 The work week`

DECLARE `work week` HAS
    `week total`       IS A NUMBER
    `frontal hours`    IS A NUMBER
    `individual hours` IS A NUMBER
    `stay hours`       IS A NUMBER

-- §4.1: a full position is 5 working days a week, even where the school
-- works 6.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-1/p1
`working days a week in a full position` MEANS 5

-- §4.4: primary special education — 36 hours: 26 frontal, 5 individual (up
-- to 3 pupils; content set by the principal under the Ministry's general
-- guidance), 5 stay hours (up to 2 of meetings; the rest adapting the
-- curriculum, parents, marking, committees, aides, outside bodies, continuity).
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-1/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-2/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-3/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_1/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p4 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p5 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p6 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p7 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p8
`the primary special-education week` MEANS `work week` 36 26 5 5
`meeting hours at most, primary` MEANS 2

-- akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p9 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p10 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p11 Where the detailed weekly table for primary special education is published (a link); no rule.

-- §4.5: health professions and arts therapists in primary special education:
-- 3 individual and 7 stay hours, two of which may serve to move between
-- institutions.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-5/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-5/p2
`the primary health-profession week` MEANS `work week` 36 26 3 7
`stay hours that may serve for moving between institutions, primary` MEANS 2

-- akn:art_4__para_4-5/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-5/p4 Where the detailed table is published (a link); no rule.

-- §4.6: post-primary special education — 36 hours: 23 frontal, 4 individual,
-- 9 stay hours (up to 4 of meetings).
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-6/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-1/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-2/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-3/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_1/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p4 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p5 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p6 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p7 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p8 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p9
`the post-primary special-education week` MEANS `work week` 36 23 4 9
`meeting hours at most, post-primary` MEANS 4

-- akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p10 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p11 Where the detailed table is published (a link); no rule.

-- §4.7: health professions and arts therapists in post-primary special
-- education: 2 individual and 11 stay hours, two for moving between them.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-7/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-7/p2
`the post-primary health-profession week` MEANS `work week` 36 23 2 11
`stay hours that may serve for moving between institutions, post-primary` MEANS 2

-- akn:art_4/p1 akn:art_4/p2 Where the detailed post-primary health-profession table is published (a link); no rule.

DECLARE `school kind` IS ONE OF
    `primary special-education school`
    `multi-stage special-education school`
    `post-primary special-education school`

DECLARE `grades taught` IS ONE OF
    `grades 1 to 6 only`
    `grades 7 to 12 only`
    `grades in both ranges`

-- §4.2–4.3: a primary special-education school (grades 1–6, 1–8 or 1–9) —
-- existing teachers on the old 30-hour or preserved 24-hour base included —
-- works the primary week (§4.4); in a multi-stage school, grades 1–6 work the
-- primary week and grades 7–12 the post-primary week (§4.6).
-- F-2019-20_tashaf_01-i: a multi-stage teacher in both ranges is not decided.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-2/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-2/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p1 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p4
GIVEN k IS A `school kind`, g IS A `grades taught`, `health profession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `work week`
DECIDE `the weeks §4 gives` k g `health profession` IS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `primary special-education school` THEN LIST `primary week`
    WHEN `post-primary special-education school` THEN LIST `post-primary week`
    WHEN `multi-stage special-education school` THEN
        CONSIDER g
        WHEN `grades 1 to 6 only`  THEN LIST `primary week`
        WHEN `grades 7 to 12 only` THEN LIST `post-primary week`
        WHEN `grades in both ranges` THEN EMPTY
    WHERE
        `primary week` MEANS
            IF `health profession` THEN `the primary health-profession week` ELSE `the primary special-education week`
        `post-primary week` MEANS
            IF `health profession` THEN `the post-primary health-profession week` ELSE `the post-primary special-education week`

§§ `5 Part positions`

-- §5.1–5.2: a special-education teacher on reform terms holds at least a
-- third of a position; a health-profession employee may hold less.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-1/p1 akn:art_5__para_5-2/p1
GIVEN t IS A `special-ed teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the position is allowed under reform terms` t IF
    t's `position fraction` AT LEAST 1 DIVIDED BY 3 OR t's `health profession or arts therapist`

-- §5.3: a part position is cut in proportion across frontal, individual and
-- stay hours; a health-profession employee under a third, or a teacher of a
-- required subject approved under a third, with 3 frontal hours or fewer,
-- teaches only "single frontal hours" — no individual or stay hours — and
-- the position is those hours over the position base.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-3/p1
GIVEN w IS A `work week`, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the part-position week` w f IS
    `work week` (w's `week total` TIMES f) (w's `frontal hours` TIMES f) (w's `individual hours` TIMES f) (w's `stay hours` TIMES f)

@ref akn:art_5__para_5-3/p2
GIVEN `a health-profession employee, or a required-subject teacher by special approval, under a third of a position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `frontal hours` IS A NUMBER
      `position base` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the position of single frontal hours` `a health-profession employee, or a required-subject teacher by special approval, under a third of a position` `frontal hours` `position base` IS
    IF `a health-profession employee, or a required-subject teacher by special approval, under a third of a position`
       AND `frontal hours` AT MOST 3
    THEN JUST (`frontal hours` DIVIDED BY `position base`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- §5.4: at most two schools, and at most 100% in all of them — except a
-- health-profession employee, or a subject the division allows in more.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-4/p1
GIVEN `number of schools` IS A NUMBER, `total position` IS A NUMBER, `exempt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the schools rule is met` `number of schools` `total position` `exempt` IF
    `exempt` OR (`number of schools` AT MOST 2 AND `total position` AT MOST 1)

-- §5.5: work under a third of a position does not count toward the minimum
-- time to promotion.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-5/p1
GIVEN t IS A `special-ed teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts toward the minimum time to promotion` t IF
    t's `position fraction` AT LEAST 1 DIVIDED BY 3

§§ `6 Above a full position`

-- §6.1–6.2: as a rule at most 100%; beyond it only exceptionally, not for
-- principals or first deputies, by the system's needs and the criteria:
-- a required subject (sciences, English, mathematics, physical education),
-- a shortage in the area, a remote locality; the extra hours frontal only;
-- at most 8.5 hours a day and 42 a week in all.
DECLARE `excess request` HAS
    `a principal or first deputy`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `required subject`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `shortage in the area`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `remote locality`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `extra hours all frontal`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours on the longest day`      IS A NUMBER
    `hours in the week`             IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_6__para_6-1/p1 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p1 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p2 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p3 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p4 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p5 akn:art_6__para_6-2/p6
GIVEN r IS AN `excess request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employment above 100% may be approved` r IF
        (NOT r's `a principal or first deputy`)
    AND (r's `required subject` OR r's `shortage in the area` OR r's `remote locality`)
    AND r's `extra hours all frontal`
    AND r's `hours on the longest day` AT MOST 8.5
    AND r's `hours in the week` AT MOST 42

-- §6.3–6.4: the placement system allows up to 117%; beyond that the request
-- goes to the division's headquarters through the entitlements system.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-3/p1 akn:art_6__para_6-4/p1
GIVEN `position asked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `approver`
DECIDE `who places a position of` `position asked` IS
    BRANCH IF `position asked` AT MOST 1    THEN `the placement system`
           IF `position asked` AT MOST 1.17 THEN `the placement system`
           OTHERWISE `the division's headquarters`

DECLARE `approver` IS ONE OF `the placement system`, `the division's headquarters`, `nobody`

§§ `7 Mothers`

DECLARE `hours relief` IS ONE OF
    `the mother's reduction`
    `the nursing hour`
    `no relief`

-- §7.1: the mother's position is set by the takanon: a mother employed at
-- 79% or more of her position.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-1/p1 akn:art_7__para_7-1/p2
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER, `a mother` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the mother's position` `position fraction` `a mother` IF
    `a mother` AND `position fraction` AT LEAST 0.79

-- §7.2: such a mother may drop one frontal hour and one stay hour from the
-- reform week (the weekly tables show her week).
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-2/p1 akn:art_7__para_7-2/p2
`frontal hours a mother drops` MEANS 1
`stay hours a mother drops` MEANS 1

-- §7.3: after maternity leave, at 90% or more, for four months: one hour a
-- day (five a week) off the stay hours, pay and position unchanged, and §7.2
-- does not apply meanwhile. §7.4: at 79% to 90%, the mother's reduction of
-- §7.2. §7.5: never both. F-2019-20_tashaf_01-c: 90% is in both clauses.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-3/p1 akn:art_7__para_7-4/p1 akn:art_7__para_7-5/p1
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER, `within four months of maternity leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `hours relief`
DECIDE `the reliefs §7 gives after maternity leave` `position fraction` `within four months of maternity leave` IS
    IF `within four months of maternity leave`
    THEN append (IF `position fraction` AT LEAST 0.9 THEN LIST `the nursing hour` ELSE EMPTY)
                (IF `position fraction` AT LEAST 0.79 AND `position fraction` AT MOST 0.9 THEN LIST `the mother's reduction` ELSE EMPTY)
    ELSE EMPTY

-- Reading adopted: at 90% the nursing hour (§7.3, "90% and more") governs,
-- §7.4's "79% to 90%" read as below 90%.
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER, `within four months of maternity leave` IS A BOOLEAN, `a mother` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `hours relief`
DECIDE `the relief` `position fraction` `within four months of maternity leave` `a mother` IS
    BRANCH IF `within four months of maternity leave` AND `position fraction` AT LEAST 0.9 THEN `the nursing hour`
           IF `entitled to the mother's position` `position fraction` (`a mother` OR `within four months of maternity leave`) THEN `the mother's reduction`
           OTHERWISE `no relief`

§§ `8 Age hours`

DECLARE `age reduction` HAS
    `frontal hours off`    IS A NUMBER
    `individual hours off` IS A NUMBER
    `base after`           IS A NUMBER

-- §8.1: the age of entitlement is unchanged from before the reform. §8.2:
-- teachers aged 50–55 drop 2 frontal hours (pro rata for a part position);
-- the base becomes 34. §8.3: EXISTING teachers aged 55 and over drop 3
-- frontal and 1 individual hour; base 32. §8.4: NEW teachers aged 55 and
-- over drop 2 frontal hours only; base 34, nothing further after 50.
-- F-2019-20_tashaf_01-d: age 55 is in §8.2 and in §8.3/8.4.
@ref akn:art_8__para_8-1/p1 akn:art_8__para_8-2/p1 akn:art_8__para_8-3/p1 akn:art_8__para_8-4/p1
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, existing IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `age reduction`
DECIDE `the reductions §8 gives` age existing IS
    append (IF age AT LEAST 50 AND age AT MOST 55 THEN LIST (`age reduction` 2 0 34) ELSE EMPTY)
           (IF age AT LEAST 55
            THEN IF existing THEN LIST (`age reduction` 3 1 32) ELSE LIST (`age reduction` 2 0 34)
            ELSE EMPTY)

-- Reading adopted: the band that opens at 55 governs age 55.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, existing IS A BOOLEAN, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `age reduction`
DECIDE `the age reduction` age existing f IS
    BRANCH IF age AT LEAST 55 AND existing THEN `age reduction` (3 TIMES f) (1 TIMES f) 32
           IF age AT LEAST 50 THEN `age reduction` (2 TIMES f) 0 34
           OTHERWISE `age reduction` 0 0 36

§§ `9 Principals and first deputies`

-- §9.1: a principal or first deputy in a reform school works exactly 100%,
-- five days. §9.2–9.3: a principal's week is 40 hours, of which 6 to 9
-- frontal by the school's complexity level, which also sets pay.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-1/p1
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a principal's or first deputy's position is allowed` `position fraction` IF
    `position fraction` EQUALS 1

@ref akn:art_9__para_9-2/p1 akn:art_9__para_9-3/p1
`a principal's week` MEANS 40

-- §9.4–9.6: eight complexity levels from the school-management index
-- (classes, kinds of disability, stages); the minimum in special education
-- is 3. Computed each May for the next year from the Ministry's data; a new
-- institution is computed in December at the minimum until then, then
-- retroactively.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-4/p1
GIVEN `computed level` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the complexity level` `computed level` IS max 3 (min `computed level` 8)

@ref akn:art_9__para_9-5/p1 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p1
GIVEN `a new institution` IS A BOOLEAN, `before the December computation` IS A BOOLEAN, `computed level` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the level in force` `a new institution` `before the December computation` `computed level` IS
    IF `a new institution` AND `before the December computation`
    THEN 3
    ELSE `the complexity level` `computed level`

-- akn:art_9__para_9-6/p4 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p5 Where the complexity computation is explained (a link); no rule.

DECLARE `level row` HAS
    `row level`        IS A NUMBER
    `row frontal hours` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN level IS A NUMBER, rows IS A LIST OF `level row`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the hours the table gives for level` level rows IS
    map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row frontal hours`) (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row level` EQUALS level) rows)

@ref akn:art_9__para_9-6/p2 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p3 akn:art_9__para_9-6/t1
`the principals' table` MEANS
    LIST `level row` 3 9, `level row` 4 8, `level row` 5 8, `level row` 6 7, `level row` 7 7, `level row` 8 6

-- §9.7: a first deputy's week is 40 hours.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7/p1
`a first deputy's week` MEANS 40

-- §9.7.1-9.7.3: a first deputy's frontal hours by school kind and level.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-1/p1 akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-1/t1
`the primary first deputies' table` MEANS
    LIST `level row` 3 21, `level row` 4 21, `level row` 5 20, `level row` 6 20, `level row` 7 19, `level row` 8 18

@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-2/p1 akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-2/t1
`the post-primary first deputies' table` MEANS
    LIST `level row` 3 11, `level row` 4 11, `level row` 5 11, `level row` 6 11, `level row` 7 9, `level row` 8 9

@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-3/p1 akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-3/t1
`the multi-stage first deputies' table` MEANS
    LIST `level row` 3 15, `level row` 4 15, `level row` 5 14, `level row` 6 14, `level row` 7 13, `level row` 8 13

-- §9.8: a second (or later) deputy works a teacher's week, the individual
-- hours on the deputy's work.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-8/p1
GIVEN w IS A `work week`
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `a second deputy's week` w IS w

-- §9.9–9.10: a principal or first deputy entitled to the mother's position,
-- and one aged 50 or more, drops two weekly non-frontal hours, pay and
-- position unchanged.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-9/p1 akn:art_9__para_9-10/p1
GIVEN `entitled as a mother` IS A BOOLEAN, age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `non-frontal hours a principal drops` `entitled as a mother` age IS
    (IF `entitled as a mother` THEN 2 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF age AT LEAST 50 THEN 2 ELSE 0)

§§ `10 School-activity hours`

-- §10.1: a teacher on reform terms, at any position, is paid for school
-- activities on top of the position and the fixed salary.
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-1/p1
GIVEN `employed on reform terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `school-activity hours are paid beyond the position` `employed on reform terms` IF
    `employed on reform terms`

-- §10.2–10.3: allotted by the school's needs, at most 18 per half-year: a
-- general school assembly (up to 4), individual parent-and-child meetings
-- (up to 8), after-hours activity (up to 6).
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-2/p1 akn:art_10__para_10-3/p1 akn:art_10__para_10-3/p2 akn:art_10__para_10-3/p3 akn:art_10__para_10-3/p4
GIVEN assembly IS A NUMBER, meetings IS A NUMBER, `after hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the half-year's activity hours are within the limits` assembly meetings `after hours` IF
        assembly AT MOST 4
    AND meetings AT MOST 8
    AND `after hours` AT MOST 6
    AND assembly PLUS meetings PLUS `after hours` AT MOST 18

§§ `11 Leaving Ofek Hadash`

-- §11.1–11.2: as a rule every eligible teacher joins; a request to leave is
-- heard only exceptionally — health of the teacher or a first-degree
-- relative (with current medical evidence), or a change for the worse in
-- personal or family circumstances since joining. §11.3–11.4: on the form of
-- annex D, through the portal.
@ref akn:art_11__para_11-1/p1 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p1 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p2 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p3 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p4 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p5
GIVEN `health ground with current medical evidence` IS A BOOLEAN, `personal circumstances worsened since joining` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a request to leave may be heard` `health ground with current medical evidence` `personal circumstances worsened since joining` IF
    `health ground with current medical evidence` OR `personal circumstances worsened since joining`

@ref akn:art_11__para_11-3/p1 akn:art_11__para_11-4/p1 akn:art_11__para_11-4/p2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `applying to leave` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MAY   `apply to leave Ofek Hadash on the annex D form`

-- akn:att_4__hc_1 Annex D, the form requesting leave from Ofek Hadash (details, request, the principal's comment, signature, link and letterhead); a form for section 11.3.

§§ `12 Promotion`

-- §12.1: promotion turns on the minimum time (פז"נ), professional-development
-- hours (שפ"מ) and evaluation, each per the Ministry's guidance (links).
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-1/p1 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p7
GIVEN `months in grade` IS A NUMBER, `development hours` IS A NUMBER, `evaluation passed` IS A BOOLEAN, row IS A `promotion row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be promoted` `months in grade` `development hours` `evaluation passed` row IF
        `months in grade` AT LEAST row's `minimum months`
    AND `development hours` AT LEAST row's `development hours required`
    AND `evaluation passed`

-- akn:art_12__para_12-1/p4 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p5 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p6 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p8 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p9 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p10 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p11 akn:art_12__para_12-1/p12 Where the development framework, the evaluation and the indicator map are published (links); no rule.

DECLARE `promotion row` HAS
    `from grade`                 IS A STRING
    `minimum months`             IS A NUMBER
    `development hours required` IS A NUMBER
    `salary increase`            IS A NUMBER @desc the increase of the table salary, as a fraction

-- §12.2.1: certified academics (teachers and kindergarten teachers).
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-2/p1 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1/p1 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1/p4 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1/p5 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-1/t1
`the certified academics' promotion table` MEANS
    LIST `promotion row` "1-2" 30 120 0.075, `promotion row` "2-3" 30 120 0.075,
         `promotion row` "3-4" 36 180 0.075, `promotion row` "4-5" 36 180 0.075,
         `promotion row` "5-6" 36 180 0.075, `promotion row` "6-7" 48 210 0.075,
         `promotion row` "7-8" 48 210 0.075, `promotion row` "8-9" 48 210 0.075

-- §12.2.2: uncertified academics. Veterans "up to 25 years" joined by
-- exception cannot advance until certified, then get the time and hours from
-- joining (one promotion) and up to 60 study hours toward שפ"מ; those of "25
-- years and over" need not certify. New ones joined by exception start
-- counting at certification. F-2019-20_tashaf_01-e: 25 years is in both.
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p1 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p4 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p5 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p6 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p7
GIVEN `seniority years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
DECIDE `what §12.2.2 says of an uncertified veteran's advance` `seniority years` IS
    append (IF `seniority years` AT MOST 25 THEN LIST FALSE ELSE EMPTY)
           (IF `seniority years` AT LEAST 25 THEN LIST TRUE ELSE EMPTY)

-- Reading adopted: §3.2.1's "below 25" governs — 25 years and over need not
-- certify.
GIVEN `seniority years` IS A NUMBER, certified IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an uncertified veteran may advance` `seniority years` certified IF
    certified OR `seniority years` AT LEAST 25

@ref akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-2/p5
`study hours counted toward development at most` MEANS 60

-- §12.2.3: certified non-academics. Up to 27 years: the degree commitment
-- (§3.3) and no promotion until the degree is proven; 28 and over: the table.
-- (F-2019-20_tashaf_01-a's gap between 27 and 28 recurs here.)
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/p1 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/p4 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/p5 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/p6 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/p7 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_12-2-3/t1
`the certified non-academics' promotion table` MEANS
    LIST `promotion row` "1-2" 48 480 0.075, `promotion row` "2-3" 48 480 0.075,
         `promotion row` "3-4" 48 480 0.075, `promotion row` "4-5" 48 480 0.075,
         `promotion row` "5-6" 48 480 0.075, `promotion row` "6-7" 48 480 0.075,
         `promotion row` "7-8" 48 480 0.075, `promotion row` "8-9" 48 480 0.075

-- §12.3: principals and deputies.
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-3/p1 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-1/p1 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-1/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-1/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-1/p4 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-1/p5 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-1/t1
`the academic principals' promotion table` MEANS
    LIST `promotion row` "א-ב" 36 210 0.0875, `promotion row` "ב-ג" 36 210 0.0875, `promotion row` "ג-ד" 36 210 0.0875

@ref akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-2/p1 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-2/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-2/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-2/p4 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-2/p5 akn:art_12__para_12-3__subpara_12-3-2/t1
`the non-academic principals' promotion table` MEANS
    LIST `promotion row` "א-ב" 48 480 0.0875, `promotion row` "ב-ג" 48 480 0.0875, `promotion row` "ג-ד" 48 480 0.0875

§§ `13 Educational counsellors`

-- §13.1: a counsellor works an academic teacher's week; the frontal hours
-- split between teaching and counselling as the principal sets; individual
-- hours are counselling; stay hours also serve counselling. In primary and
-- junior-high schools at least 1/6 of the position frontal (6 of 36), and at
-- least 4 frontal hours for any position fraction (the 1/6 is stated for
-- primary and junior-high schools; the 4 for every position).
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-1/p1 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p2 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p3 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p4 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p5 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p6 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p7 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p8 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p9
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER, `in a primary or junior-high school` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a counsellor's minimum frontal hours` `position fraction` `in a primary or junior-high school` IS
    IF `in a primary or junior-high school`
    THEN max (36 TIMES `position fraction` DIVIDED BY 6) 4
    ELSE 4

-- §13.2: new counsellors are paid on the new academic teachers' tables.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-2/p1
GIVEN `a new counsellor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `on the new academic teachers' tables` `a new counsellor` IF `a new counsellor`

-- §13.3: at least 7 counselling hours earn the counselling reward: 8% with a
-- temporary licence, 12% with a permanent one.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-3/p1 akn:art_13__para_13-3/p2 akn:art_13__para_13-3/p3
GIVEN `counselling hours` IS A NUMBER, `permanent licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the counselling reward` `counselling hours` `permanent licence` IS
    IF `counselling hours` AT LEAST 7
    THEN IF `permanent licence` THEN 0.12 ELSE 0.08
    ELSE 0

§§ `14 The Ofek Hadash grade`

-- §14.2–14.5: the grade rests on employment, education and salary data; the
-- conversion (by the Ministry's accountant) uses March of the year before
-- joining — seniority, grade, training rewards, roles, the conversion
-- supplement — and the salary a 100% position earned then; the grade may be
-- a half grade.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-2/p1 akn:art_14__para_14-3/p1 akn:art_14__para_14-4/p1 akn:art_14__para_14-5/p1
GIVEN `March salary at the actual position` IS A NUMBER, `position fraction in March` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary for conversion` `March salary at the actual position` `position fraction in March` IS
    `March salary at the actual position` DIVIDED BY `position fraction in March`

-- akn:art_14__para_14-6/p1 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p2 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p3 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p4 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p5 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p6 Notice that conversion details and conferences will follow, a pointer to annex E, and links to the salary tables and the shekel-supplement circular; no rule.

-- §14.7: role rewards; at most two. F-2019-20_tashaf_01-f: the grade
-- coordinator's "7% / 6%*" carries an asterisk the circular never explains.
DECLARE `role` IS ONE OF
    `second deputy`, `class educator`, `first-grade class educator`,
    `special-education teacher`, `subject coordinator`, `road-safety coordinator`,
    `security coordinator`, `social-education coordinator`, `grade coordinator`,
    `laboratory coordinator`, `measurement and evaluation coordinator`,
    `trips coordinator`, `inclusion coordinator`, `pedagogical coordinator`,
    `mentor of interns`

@ref akn:art_14__para_14-7/p1 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p2 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p3 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p4 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p5 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p6 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p7 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p8 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p9 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p10 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p11 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p12 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p13 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p14 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p15 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p16
GIVEN r IS A `role`, `in junior high` IS A BOOLEAN, interns IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the rates §14.7 prints for` r `in junior high` interns IS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `second deputy`                         THEN LIST 0.13
    WHEN `class educator`                        THEN LIST 0.10
    WHEN `first-grade class educator`            THEN LIST 0.115
    WHEN `special-education teacher`             THEN EMPTY
    WHEN `subject coordinator`                   THEN LIST (IF `in junior high` THEN 0.08 ELSE 0.06)
    WHEN `road-safety coordinator`               THEN LIST 0.06
    WHEN `security coordinator`                  THEN LIST 0.06
    WHEN `social-education coordinator`          THEN LIST (IF `in junior high` THEN 0.10 ELSE 0.06)
    WHEN `grade coordinator`                     THEN LIST 0.07, 0.06
    WHEN `laboratory coordinator`                THEN LIST 0.03
    WHEN `measurement and evaluation coordinator` THEN LIST 0.06
    WHEN `trips coordinator`                     THEN LIST 0.06
    WHEN `inclusion coordinator`                 THEN LIST 0.06
    WHEN `pedagogical coordinator`               THEN LIST 0.06
    WHEN `mentor of interns`                     THEN LIST (0.024 TIMES min interns 3)
-- (The special-education teacher's reward is "as customary today": not printed.)

@ref akn:art_14__para_14-7/p17
GIVEN roles IS A LIST OF `role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the role rewards are within the limit` roles IF count roles AT MOST 2

§§ `15 Salary advances until the grade is set`

-- §15.1: until the grade is set, the owner pays joined teachers an advance on
-- top of the current salary, computed on the current combined salary,
-- supplement, '87, '94, 2001, 2008 and 2011 supplements, split and training
-- rewards and double degree — for the share of employment in the joined
-- school, from joining. After the grade is set, salary is recomputed back to
-- joining and the salary and advance paid meanwhile are offset.
@ref akn:art_15__para_15-1/p1 akn:art_15__para_15-1/p2 akn:art_15__para_15-1/p3 akn:art_15__para_15-1/p4
GIVEN `salary components the advance is computed on` IS A NUMBER, rate IS A NUMBER, `share in the joined school` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Ofek Hadash advance` `salary components the advance is computed on` rate `share in the joined school` IS
    `salary components the advance is computed on` TIMES rate TIMES `share in the joined school`

GIVEN `Ofek Hadash salary back to joining` IS A NUMBER, `salary paid meanwhile` IS A NUMBER, `advances paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the retroactive settlement` `Ofek Hadash salary back to joining` `salary paid meanwhile` `advances paid` IS
    `Ofek Hadash salary back to joining` MINUS `salary paid meanwhile` MINUS `advances paid`

-- §15.2: the advance rates. Primary (and grades 1–6 of a multi-stage
-- school): 17%, interns 14%; post-primary (and grades 7 up): 27%, interns
-- 22%; first deputies 20%; principals 15%.
@ref akn:art_15__para_15-2/p1 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p2 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p3 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p4 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p5 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p6 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p7 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p8 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p9 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p10
GIVEN p IS AN `advance post`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the advance rate` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `primary teacher`      THEN 0.17
    WHEN `primary intern`       THEN 0.14
    WHEN `post-primary teacher` THEN 0.27
    WHEN `post-primary intern`  THEN 0.22
    WHEN `first deputy`         THEN 0.20
    WHEN `principal`            THEN 0.15

DECLARE `advance post` IS ONE OF
    `primary teacher`, `primary intern`, `post-primary teacher`, `post-primary intern`,
    `first deputy`, `principal`

@ref akn:art_15__para_15-1/p3
GIVEN `the advance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `paying the advance` `the advance` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the Ofek Hadash advance` `advance paid`
          PROVIDED `advance paid` AT LEAST `the advance`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תש\"ף/1 §15.1: the owner computes and pays the Ofek Hadash advance"

-- akn:art_15/p1 Notice that the reimbursement of the advance will be set in a separate circular; no rule yet.

§§ `16 The attendance clock`

-- §16.1–16.4: a clock is installed and teachers report through it; hours
-- count from clocking in and not before 7:45; until it is installed,
-- reporting is manual; the owner pays and deducts by the clock's data after
-- checking justified absences.
@ref akn:art_16__para_16-1/p1 akn:art_16__para_16-3/p1
GIVEN `the clock is installed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `reporting working hours` `the clock is installed` IS
    IF `the clock is installed`
    THEN PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MUST  `report working hours by the attendance clock`
         LEST BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "תש\"ף/1 §16.1: hours are reported by the clock"
    ELSE PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MUST  `report working hours manually`
         LEST BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "תש\"ף/1 §16.3: until the clock is installed, hours are reported manually"

-- §16.1's "a clock shall be installed" names no one; the owner, to whom the
-- circular is addressed and who pays by the clock (§16.4), is taken.
@ref akn:art_16__para_16-1/p1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `installing the clock` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `install an attendance clock`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תש\"ף/1 §16.1: an attendance clock is installed in the school"

@ref akn:art_16__para_16-2/p1
GIVEN `clock-in minute of the day` IS A NUMBER @desc minutes after midnight
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours count from minute` `clock-in minute of the day` IS
    max `clock-in minute of the day` (7 TIMES 60 PLUS 45)

@ref akn:art_16__para_16-4/p1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reform action`
DECIDE `paying by the clock` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay and deduct by the attendance clock`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תש\"ף/1 §16.4: pay and deductions follow the clock's data, after justified absences are checked"

§§ `17 The agreements prevail`

-- "17" (published inside §16 by the corpus): the circular gathers the Ofek
-- Hadash agreements' rules; where it contradicts them — for or against the
-- employee — the agreements apply.
@ref akn:art_16/p1
GIVEN `the circular's answer` IS A NUMBER, `the agreements' answer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what applies` `the circular's answer` `the agreements' answer` IS `the agreements' answer`

§§ `Annex E: grade and salary conversion`

DECLARE `reference month` IS ONE OF
    `March of the year before joining`
    `the month of joining`
    `September of the year of joining`

-- Annex E ¶1–4: an EXISTING teacher's grade is set by converting salary,
-- by personal data, role and the stage taught on the eve of joining; a NEW
-- teacher is placed directly at grade 1 by education and role, without
-- conversion (and after the internship, at seniority 1 — §1(ד)(1)).
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d__cls_1/p1
GIVEN `a new teacher` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the grade without conversion` `a new teacher` IS
    IF `a new teacher` THEN JUST 1 ELSE NOTHING

-- Annex E §1(א), §2(א), §3(א): A = X × (100 + Y)%. F-2019-20_tashaf_01-g: the
-- three worked examples multiply X by 1.034 ("תוספת שחיקה") before
-- applying Y, a factor the formula and the circular never state.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p5 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p6 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p5 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p6 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p7
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `salary after conversion` x y IS x TIMES (100 PLUS y) DIVIDED BY 100

-- Annex E §1(ב): X is what a 100% position earned in March of the year
-- before joining, in combined salary, the supplement, '87, '94, 2001, 2008
-- and 2011 supplements, and the rewards that end with the reform (split,
-- training, in-service training, double degree, cost of living); with no
-- March employment, the month of joining. §1(ד)(2), §2(ג), §3(ג): one on
-- unpaid leave or sabbatical takes September of the year of joining.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p5
`the components X is computed on` MEANS
    LIST "שכר משולב", "תוספת '87", "תוספת '94", "תוספת 2001", "תוספת 2008", "תוספת 2011",
         "גמול פיצול", "גמול הכשרות", "גמול השתלמות", "גמול כפל תואר", "תוספת יוקר"

@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p6 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d__cls_2/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p3
GIVEN `employed in that March` IS A BOOLEAN, `on unpaid leave or sabbatical the year before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `reference month`
DECIDE `the month X is taken from` `employed in that March` `on unpaid leave or sabbatical the year before` IS
    BRANCH IF `on unpaid leave or sabbatical the year before` THEN `September of the year of joining`
           IF `employed in that March`                         THEN `March of the year before joining`
           OTHERWISE `the month of joining`

-- Annex E §1: Y for academic teachers is a table of coefficients by stage and
-- status (regular, mother, educator, educator + mother). The corpus does not
-- carry it (the PDF prints it as an image); only the example's value, 34 for
-- a mother in junior high, is in the text. Non-academics take 0.8 of the
-- academics' coefficient; primary-school teachers of grades 7–9 on a 24-hour
-- base take 12.5% more, and work the primary week.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p7
@desc The conversion coefficient Y for an academic teacher, from annex E's table, which the corpus does not carry.
ASSUME `the academic conversion coefficient` IS A FUNCTION FROM STRING TO NUMBER

-- akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p8 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p9 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p10 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p11 The letterhead of the next page; no rule.

@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p12 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p13 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p14
GIVEN `academic coefficient` IS A NUMBER, academic IS A BOOLEAN, `primary grades 7-9 on a 24-hour base` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the conversion coefficient` `academic coefficient` academic `primary grades 7-9 on a 24-hour base` IS
    `academic coefficient`
    TIMES (IF academic THEN 1 ELSE 0.8)
    TIMES (IF `primary grades 7-9 on a 24-hour base` THEN 1.125 ELSE 1)

-- Annex E §1(ג)–(ד), §2(ה), §3(ה): placement in the combined-salary table at
-- the grade whose salary is closest to A — "equal to it or higher".
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_c/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_e/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_e/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p2
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, `table salary of the grade placed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the placement follows the rule` a `table salary of the grade placed` IF
    `table salary of the grade placed` AT LEAST a

-- Annex E §2(ב)–(ג): a first deputy's Y is 20%; X is the March salary of a
-- 100% position less education reward, expenses, sundry payments, tax
-- gross-up and imputed benefit. §3(ב)–(ג): a principal's Y is 15%; X less
-- expenses, yearly payments, gross-up and imputed benefit.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_b/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_b/p2
`a first deputy's conversion coefficient` MEANS 20

@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p2
`what a first deputy's X leaves out` MEANS
    LIST "גמול חינוך", "החזרי הוצאות", "תשלומים שונים", "גילום מס", "זקיפת הטבה למס"

@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_b/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_b/p2
`a principal's conversion coefficient` MEANS 15

@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p2
`what a principal's X leaves out` MEANS
    LIST "החזרי הוצאות", "תשלומים שנתיים", "גילום מס", "זקיפת הטבה למס"

-- Annex E §3(ה): a principal employed above 100% (to 150%) gets a personal
-- supplement: B = T × (100 + Y)/100, where T is the March salary of the whole
-- position; C = B − the new table salary, turned into a percentage of the
-- combined salary. The month for one on leave is the March before the leave.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p5 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p6 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p7 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p8 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p9 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p10 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p11 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p12 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p13 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p14 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p15
GIVEN t IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER, `new table salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the principal's personal supplement` t y `new table salary` IS
    t TIMES (100 PLUS y) DIVIDED BY 100 MINUS `new table salary`

GIVEN c IS A NUMBER, `combined salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the personal supplement as a percentage` c `combined salary` IS c DIVIDED BY `combined salary`

-- The worked examples, as printed. A teacher (mother, junior high, 0.9 of a
-- position): components summing to 6,105.38; X = 6,783.75; × 1.034 =
-- 7,014.39; Y = 34; A = 9,399.29; placed at grade 6, 9,670.70.
